</ul><h1>Small But Mighty</h1><p>In the waning hours of trick-or-treat night, a young Dracula and a ghost converged <a href="https://meh.com/deals/pick-your-80-pack-kind-healthy-grains-energy-bars">once again</a> on a street corner to compare hauls and discuss strategy.</p>
<p>“So, no full-sized bars as of yet,” said the ghost. “But there were some fresh baked brownies at the Millers.”</p>
<p>“Oh, cool,” said Dracula. “Just a word to the wise, the Johnsons’ yard is decorated like crazy, but their selection is pretty weak. Same lollipops they give away at the grocery store.”</p>
<p>“Ah, very useful information, thank you,” said the ghost. “As for Mr. Vincent’s–”</p>
<p>“Dude, what? Mr. Vincent?” Dracula nearly dropped his treat basket. “After last year? When he gave away ‘Healthy Grains Energy Bars’? And dead fidget spinners for years before that? You seriously went back? AGAIN?”</p>
<p>“He’d set up a lawn chair basically <em>on</em> the sidewalk,” the ghost said. “I couldn’t avoid him. But it’s not as bad as it was last year. KIND minis. Dark chocolate or caramel almond and sea salt.”</p>
<p>“I guess that’s better than fruit,” said Dracula.</p>
<p>“And he says the chocolate and caramel only melted a little in the August heat,” the ghost said.</p>
<p>“Wait, huh? The August heat?”</p>
<p>“Yeah,” the ghost said. “Apparently, the deal site he ordered them from delivered while he was out of town. He was ‘down south’ to ‘play the Labubu market’? I didn’t ask follow-ups, and luckily he didn’t say anything, only sort of stared into the distance with an expression on his face like he was in pain.”</p>
<p>“But, dude,” Dracula said, “it’s October.”</p>
<p>“Oh right. August was when he ordered them,” the ghost said. “But he assured me there’s still a month before their best-by date. And I said, well, I’ll be sure to eat it before Thanksgiving. And that was a mistake because he launched into this whole thing about how what’s really scary is the general population’s lack of understanding regarding best-by dates versus expiration dates. He talked so long that my flashlight died, but he gave me another one.”</p>
<p>“He just gave you a flashlight?” Dracula said.</p>
<p>“Yeah,” the ghost said. “He told me the same site that sold the bars sells a lot of them, and ‘you can never have too many lights.’ It was weird. But the KIND bars might be good.”</p>
<p>“Yeah, I’ll think about it,” Dracula said. “Good luck on the rest of your night.”</p>
<p>“You too,” said the ghost.</p>
<p>And they parted ways.</p>